# The REINVENT 4 plugin's environment: REINVENT 4, which samples new
# molecules from a trained generative model, for its job (generate_job.py).
# Set up only when the plugin is added (docs/PLUGINS.md); its prior - the
# trained model - is downloaded besides, by Meno (manifest.json, `downloads`).
#
# REINVENT 4 installed from its repository at the commit of its release 4.8,
# pinned by the archive's hash: it is published on no package index. Resolved
# as its own installer resolves it, with pip (which leaves out the
# CUDA index its pyproject names for torch: --no-sources), from the package
# index's torch.
#
# Locked for macOS on Apple silicon, 14 or later - torch's wheels are built
# for no earlier - and Windows on x64 (manifest.json,
# `systems`), with hashes; one lock for both, each system's packages by its
# markers. Torch is the package index's: on Windows, its build for the CPU.
# Torch's GPU libraries for Linux are left out (--no-emit-package each;
# installed with --no-deps). Remade from the lock as it was, so that the
# packages macOS had keep their versions:
#   uv pip compile --universal --no-sources --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes \
#     --no-emit-package <each of torch's Linux GPU libraries> requirements.in -o requirements.lock
reinvent @ https://github.com/MolecularAI/REINVENT4/archive/80a8d21aefd9c0d3ec806377522effb30cfca12a.tar.gz
# imported by REINVENT 4 (reinvent/runmodes/utils/plot.py), and added for it
scipy
